{
  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 20,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.269,
            0.09,
            0.431,
            0.112
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "At a Glance"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.255,
            0.121,
            0.632,
            0.139
          ],
          "content": "y Sound is produced by vibrating objects."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.255,
            0.139,
            0.888,
            0.156
          ],
          "content": "y Sound is a longitudinal mechanical wave that needs a medium to travel."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.255,
            0.158,
            0.767,
            0.175
          ],
          "content": "y Sound can propagate through solids, liquids and gases."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.255,
            0.176,
            0.89,
            0.227
          ],
          "content": "In sound propagation, it is the density disturbance that travels and not the particles of the medium. The particles of the medium only vibrate about their mean positions as the sound wave passes."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.255,
            0.228,
            0.89,
            0.261
          ],
          "content": "The distance between the two consecutive crests or two consecutive troughs is called the wavelength of a wave."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.255,
            0.262,
            0.89,
            0.312
          ],
          "content": "The change in density of the medium at a fixed point, from maximum to minimum, and then again to the maximum (or vice versa), makes one complete oscillation."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.255,
            0.314,
            0.89,
            0.348
          ],
          "content": "The number of density oscillations at a fixed point per unit time is the frequency of the sound wave."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.255,
            0.349,
            0.89,
            0.383
          ],
          "content": "The time taken for one complete density oscillation at a fixed point is defined as the time period of the wave."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.364,
            0.185,
            0.578
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_20_image_9.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.256,
            0.383,
            0.89,
            0.418
          ],
          "content": "The amplitude of a sound wave is the maximum change in air density in a compression (or a rarefaction) compared to the average density."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.256,
            0.419,
            0.89,
            0.469
          ],
          "content": "The amount of sound energy passing through a unit area perpendicular to the direction of the propagation of sound wave in a unit time is called the intensity of sound."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.255,
            0.47,
            0.89,
            0.505
          ],
          "content": "The speed of sound can be defined as the distance which a point on a wave, such as a crest (or a trough), travels in unit time."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.255,
            0.505,
            0.891,
            0.539
          ],
          "content": "Echoes and reverberations are heard because of the reflection of sound from various surfaces."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.256,
            0.54,
            0.89,
            0.591
          ],
          "content": "Sound waves with frequency below 20 Hz are called infrasonic waves. Sound waves with frequency above 20 kHz are called ultrasonic waves."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.468,
            0.656,
            0.775,
            0.679
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Revise, Reflect, Refine"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.237,
            0.713,
            0.888,
            0.747
          ],
          "content": "1. Which observation best supports the idea that sound is a mechanical wave?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.272,
            0.75,
            0.52,
            0.768
          ],
          "content": "(i) Sound shows reflection"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.266,
            0.768,
            0.636,
            0.786
          ],
          "content": "(ii) Sound needs a medium to propagate"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.262,
            0.785,
            0.5,
            0.802
          ],
          "content": "(iii) Sound has frequency"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.263,
            0.802,
            0.501,
            0.819
          ],
          "content": "(iv) Sound carries energy"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.236,
            0.822,
            0.887,
            0.856
          ],
          "content": "2. For a sound wave propagating in a medium, increasing its frequency will increase its"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.273,
            0.86,
            0.416,
            0.878
          ],
          "content": "(i) wavelength"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.268,
            0.877,
            0.364,
            0.894
          ],
          "content": "(ii) speed"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.262,
            0.893,
            0.633,
            0.911
          ],
          "content": "(iii) number of compressions per second"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.264,
            0.911,
            0.416,
            0.928
          ],
          "content": "(iv) time period"
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.074,
